  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe SPS for elevated risk of fire spread for the Hudson Valley,\nUpper Hudson Valley and Catskills expired at 6 pm. Gusty west \nto northwest winds will continue to diminish early this evening \nwith the skies becoming partly cloudy to mostly clear. Lows will\nbe much colder than last night with mid 20s to lower 30s over \nthe higher terrain...and mid and upper 30s in the valleys. \nNorthwest to north winds will generally be 10 mph or less\nshortly before or just after midnight. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nOutside of a few evening showers/sprinkles across portions of\nthe SW Adirondacks, generally dry conditions are expected\nthrough the weekend and into the middle of next week. Chances \nfor rain increase later next week ahead of an approaching \nfrontal system and upper level trough, however there remains \nuncertainty regarding whether upper level systems phase and \nresult in a widespread soaking rain, or the systems remain \nseparate, allowing for a more limited chance for showers.",
